                [
                    'type' => 'cta',
                    'text' => 'Request a Callback',
                ],
                [
                    'type' => 'h2',
                    'text' => 'Why Rocky Mount Crawl Spaces Take On Water',
                ],
                [
                    'type' => 'p',
                    'text' => 'Most homes across Rocky Mount, Nashville, Tarboro and the rest of the Twin Counties are built over a vented crawl space. It keeps the floor off damp ground, but it also creates a place where water can sit unseen. The most common causes we find are:',
                ],
                [
                    'type' => 'bullet',
                    'items' => [
                        [
                            'text' => 'Plumbing leaks. Supply lines, drain lines and toilet flanges under bathrooms and kitchens drip or burst straight into the crawl space.',
                        ],
                        [
                            'text' => 'Water heaters. Tanks in closets or the crawl space itself rust through and empty onto the ground.',
                        ],
                        [
                            'text' => 'AC condensate. Clogged drain lines and sweating ductwork add gallons of water every day during a long cooling season.',
                        ],
                        [
                            'text' => 'Storm runoff. Heavy summer thunderstorms and hurricane rain flow toward the house when downspouts are short or the yard slopes the wrong way.',
                        ],
                        [
                            'text' => 'High groundwater. Low-lying areas near the Tar River and Stoney Creek can see water seep up from below after long rainy stretches.',
                        ],
                        [
                            'text' => 'River and creek flooding. In bigger events, outside flood water fills crawl spaces completely.',
                        ],
                        [
                            'text' => 'Humid air. Open vents pull in muggy outdoor air that condenses on cooler joists and ducts.',
                        ],
                        [
                            'text' => 'Clay soils. Heavy clay holds water against foundation walls and drains slowly after rain.',
                        ],
                    ],
                ],
                [
                    'type' => 'h2',
                    'text' => 'Signs of Water Under Your Rocky Mount Home',
                ],
                [
                    'type' => 'p',
                    'text' => 'Most people do not crawl under their homes very often, so water damage down there usually announces itself in other ways:',
                ],
                [
                    'type' => 'bullet',
                    'items' => [
                        [
                            'text' => 'A musty or earthy smell inside the house, especially when the AC kicks on',
                        ],
                        [
                            'text' => 'Floors that feel soft, bouncy or spongy',
                        ],
                        [
                            'text' => 'Hardwood or laminate that cups, gaps or buckles',
                        ],
                        [
                            'text' => 'Vinyl flooring lifting or bubbling at the seams',
                        ],
                        [
                            'text' => 'Higher humidity indoors and condensation on windows',
                        ],
                        [
                            'text' => 'A jump in your water bill or the sound of running water with every faucet off',
                        ],
                        [
                            'text' => 'Insulation hanging down or lying on the ground when you look through the access door',
                        ],
                        [
                            'text' => 'More bugs than usual, including termite swarmers in spring',
                        ],
                    ],
                ],
                [
                    'type' => 'p',
                    'text' => 'If you notice two or more of these, it is worth a look under the house.',
                ],
                [
                    'type' => 'h2',
                    'text' => 'Is Water in a Crawl Space an Emergency in Rocky Mount?',
                ],
                [
                    'type' => 'p',
                    'text' => 'Short answer: yes, standing water in a crawl space should be treated as urgent. In Rocky Mount\'s warm, humid climate, wet insulation, joists and subfloor can start growing mold within 24 to 48 hours, and wood that stays wet begins to weaken. Have the water pumped out and the space dried by an experienced crew as soon as you find it.',
                ],
                [
                    'type' => 'p',
                    'text' => 'If you have just discovered water under your house, shut off the main water if a pipe could be the cause, avoid going under the house if water is near wiring or the HVAC unit, and turn off the HVAC system if ducts are sitting in water.',
                ],
                [
                    'type' => 'h2',
                    'text' => 'Our Crawl Space Water Damage Process in Rocky Mount',
                ],
                [
                    'type' => 'steps',
                    'steps' => [
                        [
                            'n' => 1,
                            'text' => 'Safe inspection. We check for live wiring, gas lines and HVAC equipment near the water before anyone goes under the house, then map moisture in joists, sill plates and the subfloor.',
                        ],
                        [
                            'n' => 2,
                            'text' => 'Stop the source. We locate the leak or entry point and coordinate a plumber or HVAC technician if needed.',
                        ],
                        [
                            'n' => 3,
                            'text' => 'Pump and extract. Submersible pumps and crawl space extraction tools remove standing water, even from low corners and around piers.',
                        ],
                        [
                            'n' => 4,
                            'text' => 'Remove what cannot be saved. Soaked fiberglass insulation, a torn or contaminated vapor barrier and debris are bagged and hauled out.',
                        ],
                        [
                            'n' => 5,
                            'text' => 'Clean and treat. The soil surface, piers, joists and subfloor are cleaned and treated with an antimicrobial to slow mold and odor.',
                        ],
                        [
                            'n' => 6,
                            'text' => 'Dry. Low-grain refrigerant dehumidifiers and air movers run under the house, often with foundation vents closed temporarily so humid outdoor air does not undo the work. Rooms above are dried at the same time.',
                        ],
                        [
                            'n' => 7,
                            'text' => 'Verify. We take wood moisture readings every day until joists, sill plates and subfloor reach their dry goal.',
                        ],
                        [
                            'n' => 8,
                            'text' => 'Restore. New insulation and a new vapor barrier go in, and we recommend any drainage or moisture control changes that would help.',
                        ],
                    ],
                ],
                [
                    'type' => 'h2',
                    'text' => 'What Happens to Rocky Mount Joists, Subfloors and Insulation When They Stay Wet',
                ],
                [
                    'type' => 'p',
                    'text' => 'The crawl space is the structural heart of most Eastern Carolina homes, and wet wood under the house causes problems that show up upstairs.',
                ],
                [
                    'type' => 'p',
                    'text' => 'Fiberglass insulation between the joists soaks up water, sags and holds that water directly against the subfloor. Wood that stays above roughly 19 percent moisture content is at risk of decay and mold growth, and in a warm crawl space that can happen within days. Sill plates sitting on the foundation wick moisture and can start to rot. Damp wood also attracts termites, which are already active across Nash and Edgecombe counties.',
                ],
                [
                    'type' => 'p',
                    'text' => 'Upstairs, you may notice hardwood or laminate floors cupping, vinyl lifting at the seams, doors sticking, or a musty smell. Air from the crawl space naturally rises into the living space, so whatever is growing under the house ends up in the air your family breathes. Drying the crawl space properly protects both the structure and your indoor air.',
                ],
                [
                    'type' => 'h2',
                    'text' => 'Wet Ductwork in Rocky Mount Crawl Spaces',
                ],
                [
                    'type' => 'p',
                    'text' => 'In most Rocky Mount homes, the heating and cooling ducts run through the crawl space. That makes them part of every crawl space water job.',
                ],
                [
                    'type' => 'p',
                    'text' => 'In summer, cold ducts in a humid crawl space sweat. Drops of condensation fall onto insulation and the vapor barrier, and over a season they can soak an area as badly as a slow leak. If a duct is crushed, disconnected or poorly insulated, the problem gets worse.',
                ],
                [
                    'type' => 'p',
                    'text' => 'When standing water or flood water reaches the ducts, the inside of the duct can become contaminated. Running the system then blows damp, musty air into every room. If ducts were touched by water, we recommend turning the HVAC system off until they are inspected. Flex duct that was submerged is usually replaced, while metal duct can often be cleaned and sanitized. We will tell you which applies and coordinate with your HVAC company if repairs are needed.',
